The paper determines the minimal embedding dimension D_g(f) for embedding a periodic map f of order n ≥ 3g on a closed oriented surface of genus g into spheres, in the smooth and orientation-preserving category. Specifically, it shows that when n ≥ 3g and g > 0, D_g(f) = 6 with a few exceptions explicitly described. Furthermore, for any integer m > 1, it constructs infinitely many periodic maps f such that D_g(f) = m.
